<h2 class="doc-h2">Destructive</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The colour belongs to the thing that does the damage, not to the thing that opens the
    question — which is why the recipe is on the action and not on the trigger.
</p>
<Example Source="AlertDialogDestructive.razor"><AlertDialogDestructive /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Confirming an existing control</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>data-ask</code> on any button or link builds this on the fly, with no markup in the page
    at all — which is what makes it usable on a row in a table where writing a dialog per row
    would be absurd.
</p>
<Example Source="AskExample.razor"><AskExample /></Example>

